{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzmzSDrQbC5AUYUknjxR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Answer: You need both manager approval and finance approval before the purchase goes ahead.**\n\n**Why:**\n\n1. **Which limit applies.** The purchase date is October 12, 2026, which is after July 1, 2025. So the current $2,500 routine limit applies, not the older $2,000 limit (AMD-2, DEF-3).\n2. **Which rule applies.** $2,600 is more than $2,500. A routine non-travel purchase above $2,500 needs **both manager and finance approval before purchase** (EXP-2). The $2,600 counts the full transaction, including taxes and fees (EXP-4).\n3. **Emergency waiver doesn't apply.** The request is described as routine and nothing suggests an emergency (DEF-1), so the waiver of advance finance approval isn't available (EMG-2). Even in a real emergency, manager approval would still be needed (EXP-3, EMG-1).\n4. **No travel-office approval.** This isn't airfare or travel, so the Travel Policy doesn't apply (TRV-1).\n\n**One thing to check:** Vendor restrictions always apply (EXP-3), and the request doesn't say which vendor is being used. If the vendor is on the prohibited list, the purchase can't go ahead without specific **written authorization from the compliance officer**. Manager and finance approval don't count as that authorization (VEN-1, VEN-2). If the vendor isn't prohibited, manager and finance approval are all you need."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_read_input_tokens":5715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2359},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7253533d-cceb-4f04-9cf0-e77ec253becb","uuid":"cdae55e9-5721-435